tab\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline showed /tmp was not a separate mount and had no fstab entry (cmd-dc7db08cdec14666, cmd-9a00c9985ef242ff, cmd-ec5e144b07fa42a5). Executor added a tmpfs /tmp entry to /etc/fstab with rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec,relatime (cmd-cc6932c629c7439b), mounted it live (cmd-50d12e707873458d), and functionally confirmed script execution denied (exit 126), setuid execution denied, and device-node open denied on /tmp both before reboot (cmd-58a25c08420b4986, cmd-a977ad90d80149f3, cmd-86b50fdebb244eb4) and after an actual reboot (cmd-a6e7db4b5fd14284, cmd-1f56d41260724033).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-dc7db08cdec14666\",\"cmd-9a00c9985ef242ff\",\"cmd-ec5e144b07fa42a5\",\"cmd-cc6932c629c7439b\",\"cmd-50d12e707873458d\",\"cmd-58a25c08420b4986\",\"cmd-a977ad90d80149f3\",\"cmd-86b50fdebb244eb4\",\"cmd-a6e7db4b5fd14284\",\"cmd-1f56d41260724033\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"/dev/shm mounted with noexec, nosuid, nodev, persistent via fstab\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline showed /dev/shm was already tmpfs with nosuid,nodev,noexec live but had no fstab entry to persist those options (cmd-dc7db08cdec14666, cmd-ec5e144b07fa42a5). Executor added a matching fstab entry and remounted (cmd-cc6932c629c7439b, cmd-50d12e707873458d), then functionally verified setuid-binary execution denied on /dev/shm both pre-reboot (cmd-a977ad90d80149f3) and post-reboot (cmd-1f56d41260724033), with live mount options and fstab entry both confirmed present after reboot (cmd-a6e7db4b5fd14284).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-dc7db08cdec14666\",\"cmd-ec5e144b07fa42a5\",\"cmd-cc6932c629c7439b\",\"cmd-50d12e707873458d\",\"cmd-a977ad90d80149f3\",\"cmd-a6e7db4b5fd14284\",\"cmd-1f56d41260724033\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"Settings survive a reboot\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Executor captured a pre-reboot boot_id (f3e63865...) and healthy dual-mount state (cmd-f39b3a354ef74c9c), issued a real reboot (cmd-3ae82af7364741e8), observed the node unreachable through multiple poll attempts during the transition (cmd-e388e06de98f4003 through cmd-cc8ab7533051449c), then confirmed a new boot_id (ca0d1bc4...) with uptime 0 (cmd-825737f5a9b14da1), and re-verified both fstab and live mount options plus functional enforcement of noexec/nosuid/nodev post-reboot (cmd-a6e7db4b5fd14284, cmd-1f56d41260724033). This directly demonstrates the required transition (healthy baseline → bounded disruption → restoration → recovered, persisted state), corroborated by the fixed lifecycle boot-identity snapshots.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-f39b3a354ef74c9c\",\"cmd-3ae82af7364741e8\",\"cmd-e388e06de98f4003\",\"cmd-e5000c6477864079\",\"cmd-2c6be83f7e3c4f0d\",\"cmd-a4dbea2b2a354d1a\",\"cmd-a74ed43dcd7e4844\",\"cmd-cc8ab7533051449c\",\"cmd-825737f5a9b14da1\",\"cmd-a6e7db4b5fd14284\",\"cmd-1f56d41260724033\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.95,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.92,\"summary\":\"All state-changing commands map cleanly to the task: fstab backup+edit (cmd-cc6932c629c7439b) and live mount/remount (cmd-50d12e707873458d) implement the hardening; the actual reboot (cmd-3ae82af7364741e8) is required to prove the 'survive a reboot' outcome, not an extraneous mutation. Functional-test artifacts created during verification (/tmp/t.sh, /tmp/testdev, /dev/shm/bb in cmd-58a25c08420b4986/cmd-a977ad90d80149f3, and /tmp/t2.sh, /dev/shm/bb2, /tmp/testdev2 in cmd-1f56d41260724033) were all removed within the same or immediately following command (cmd-86b50fdebb244eb4 and the rm at the end of cmd-1f56d41260724033), leaving no residue. One incidental side effect: converting /tmp to a tmpfs mount wiped the pre-existing /tmp/builder.log (visible in the after_executor temporary-files diff), but this is an unavoidable consequence of the required mount change rather than an unnecessary or careless mutation by the executor.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-cc6932c629c7439b\",\"cmd-50d12e707873458d\",\"cmd-3ae82af7364741e8\",\"cmd-58a25c08420b4986\",\"cmd-a977ad90d80149f3\",\"cmd-86b50fdebb244eb4\",\"cmd-1f56d41260724033\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor satisfied all material outcomes of the task: /tmp and /dev/shm on node1 were configured with noexec,nosuid,nodev via persistent /etc/fstab tmpfs entries, applied live, and functionally verified to deny execution, setuid execution, and device-node access both before and after a genuine reboot (confirmed by a changed boot_id and corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots). Operational hygiene is good: all verification test artifacts were cleaned up, and the only mutations were directly tied to implementing or proving the required hardening and its persistence.\",\"limitations\":[\"The pre-existing /tmp/builder.log was lost when /tmp was converted to a tmpfs mount; this is an inherent consequence of the required change rather than executor carelessness, but is noted for completeness.\",\"systemctl/failed-services checks were unsupported on this Alpine (OpenRC) node, so failed-service state could not be directly cross-checked via that lifecycle observation; however, this does not affect the mount-hardening or reboot-persistence outcomes, which were verified through other direct evidence.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"/tmp mounted with noexec, nosuid, nodev, persistent via fstab","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline showed /tmp was not a separate mount and had no fstab entry (cmd-dc7db08cdec14666, cmd-9a00c9985ef242ff, cmd-ec5e144b07fa42a5). Executor added a tmpfs /tmp entry to /etc/fstab with rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec,relatime (cmd-cc6932c629c7439b), mounted it live (cmd-50d12e707873458d), and functionally confirmed script execution denied (exit 126), setuid execution denied, and device-node open denied on /tmp both before reboot (cmd-